From cb7292d4a2a4b7f4a87cdda3eaecfae209be0538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:56:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] feat(backend): record RealSense depth as LeRobot depth
 features

A RealSense camera with output_type "depth" or "both" now records its depth
map, aligned to its color image, as observation.images.<camera>_depth next to
observation.images.<camera>: a LeRobot 0.6 depth feature (shape [H, W, 1],
info.is_depth_map, depth_unit mm). "color" records exactly as before.

- Store: image slots carry a dtype; depth slots are uint16 millimetres.
- Camera worker: unpacks color and depth, writes both with the frameset's
  timestamp, zeroes depth outside depth_range_min/max, resizes depth with
  nearest neighbour, and polls at twice the camera rate.
- Recorder: rereads a color/depth pair whose timestamps differ, so both come
  from one frameset.
- Encoding: depth is 12-bit log-quantized over 0-10 m (0 stays 0, steps of
  1.3 mm at 0.3 m to 2.1 mm at 3 m) and encoded as lossless HEVC gray12le with
  the ultrafast preset; DEPTH_VIDEO_CRF switches to lossy. A dataset that has
  depth keeps the quantization it was recorded with when appended to, and a
  backend without a 12-bit HEVC encoder refuses depth clearly. RGB-only
  datasets keep the placeholder depth encoder.
- Viewing: episodes flag depth videos; the video endpoint serves a colorized,
  browser-playable copy with the same timestamps (depth_preview=true, cached);
  depth thumbnails are colorized and the default thumbnail is a color camera.
- Sessions show a depth-only camera's colorized depth and skip the depth
  frames of cameras that also have color; camera claims include the output
  type, as a publisher serves one at a time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
